<title>MEXICO: Abaco raises EPS for Mexico's Soriana.</title>
<headline>Abaco raises EPS for Mexico's Soriana.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokerage Abaco-Rodman said Wednesday it raised its 1996 and 1997 earnings per share estimates for Mexican retailer Soriana.</p>
<p>The brokerage lifted its earnings estimate to 1.054 pesos from 1.015 pesos per share for 1996, and to 1.192 pesos from 1.122 pesos per share in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We continue to see the recovery trend in the Mexican retail activity, with greater recovery in the border area,&quot; analyst Luis Miranda wrote in the brokerage report.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
